{"parentUuid":"997d0fa3-1dd3-4830-a8fe-bcfe8ae66ffb","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffebZHjJNjokAaeko8R6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NF2bsbeJyTgsr8SNaXGdpT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd spec/capabilities; cat hook-common-payload.yaml hook-timeout.yaml hooks-all-matching-run.yaml"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":673,"cache_read_input_tokens":54287,"output_tokens":118,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":24},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":673},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":118,"cache_read_input_tokens":54287,"cache_creation_input_tokens":673,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":673,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NF2bsbeJyTgsr8SNaXGdpT":{"command":"cd spec/capabilities; cat hook-common-payload.yaml hook-timeout.yaml hooks-all-matching-run.yaml"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffebZ1cBJSj7h5jJ3sEk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"4e24c971-bf2d-46f1-9ac5-4c09edb439d7","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:51:02.832Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"4e24c971-bf2d-46f1-9ac5-4c09edb439d7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NF2bsbeJyTgsr8SNaXGdpT","type":"tool_result","content":"statement: >-\n  Every lifecycle hook receives a payload naming the session, its transcript\n  file and its working directory. An event raised inside a sub-agent also\n  names that sub-agent, while events on the main thread name none.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#common-input-fields\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookmix\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#common-input-fields\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-matchers\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-end\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock has no sub-agents (its tool executor handles only the shell tool), so the events a sub-agent raises, which Codex gives the parent session's id and an agent id, are not modeled; every event is a main-thread event.\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#common-schema\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/tool-failure\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock has no sub-agents (no Task tool and no subagentStart or\n          subagentStop event), so the payload fields that name a sub-agent are not\n          modeled.\nstatement: >-\n  A hook is bounded by a timeout; when it expires, the hook and every process\n  it spawned are killed, whatever it printed is discarded, and the event\n  carries on. (How long a hook with no timeout of its own may run is the\n  harness's default for the event. Hooks run in the background, and the\n  handler kinds that are neither a command nor an endpoint, are not part of\n  this.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#timeouts\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#common-fields\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock defines and fires none of the PreModelSwitch,\n          PostModelSwitch and MessageDisplay events, so the shorter default\n          timeouts the docs give them (30 s, 30 s and 10 s), and a timed-out\n          PreModelSwitch hook blocking the model switch, are not modeled. The\n          mcp_tool hook handler is not implemented either, so a timed-out\n          mcp_tool hook's cancellation and discarded output are not modeled.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          A timed-out PreToolUse hook lets the call fall through to the normal\n          permission flow. The mock models a non-interactive run with no\n          permission rules evaluated beside the hook, so what a deny or ask\n          rule does after a timeout is not modeled.\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#config-shape\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          Codex also gives the Interrupt event a default of 1 second, capped at 3, but the mock fires no Interrupt event (a non-interactive run has nothing to interrupt), so that default is not modeled.\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#per-script-configuration-options\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout\nstatement: >-\n  Every hook that matches an event runs, all together, even when one of them\n  blocks; when several block, the harness acts on the one that finishes last or\n  merges them. The same hook configured in several settings files runs once,\n  in a harness that reads more than one. (How the decisions and the context of\n  several hooks combine is each decision's and context's own capability.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#hook-handler-fields\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks-guide#combine-results-from-multiple-hooks\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/all-hooks\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/all-hooks-slow-first\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#where-codex-looks-for-hooks\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#pretooluse\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-decisions\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hooks-all-matching-run-blockers-slow-first\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hooks-all-matching-run-blockers-fast-first\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hooks-all-matching-run-same-hook-two-files\n    deviations:\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          When several hooks block one call, Codex acts on neither the one that\n          finishes last nor a merge: it acts on the first in configuration\n          order, whichever finishes first, after all of them have run to\n          completion (recorded: a slow and a fast hook that both deny, in\n          either order, and the reason told is the first configured's), and the\n          mock does the same.\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          Codex does not run a hook configured in several settings files once:\n          the same command in the user layer's and the project layer's\n          hooks.json runs once per file, twice in all (recorded:\n          runs/hooks-all-matching-run-same-hook-two-files), and the mock does\n          the same.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock reads hooks only from the user's and the project's\n          hooks.json: the inline [hooks] tables of config.toml (user and\n          project), plugin-bundled hooks and managed hooks, which Codex also\n          loads and runs beside them, are not modeled.\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#configuration\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hooks-together\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock reads only the project's .cursor/hooks.json: the user, team\n          and enterprise sources, and so a hook configured in more than one, are\n          not modeled.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fcf6e3af-933d-4d52-8c9c-4bcf5c88fe6b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:51:04.596Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4e24c971-bf2d-46f1-9ac5-4c09edb439d7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
