{"parentUuid":"0f8ba067-b66e-46b4-a979-01282028f875","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffebpNbGcLB6qKaoNvvM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YJFMUAjeHWM7erWfRFk4bt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd spec/capabilities; cat hook-exit-code-semantics.yaml session-end-hook.yaml posttooluse-payload.yaml stop-hook-payload.yaml user-prompt-submit-hook.yaml"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2390,"cache_read_input_tokens":54960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2390,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YJFMUAjeHWM7erWfRFk4bt":{"command":"cd spec/capabilities; cat hook-exit-code-semantics.yaml session-end-hook.yaml posttooluse-payload.yaml stop-hook-payload.yaml user-prompt-submit-hook.yaml"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cffebp6xTq2o8r1zhp3QH","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"bae38a40-3d47-4493-bd0f-e501565b0fe6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:51:07.043Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"bae38a40-3d47-4493-bd0f-e501565b0fe6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffebpNbGcLB6qKaoNvvM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HDB2NQv1N1xjwkdxxtfYYN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"which sr-checks; sr-checks run --help 2>&1 | head -30; ls ~/.local/share/cursor-agent/versions/"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2390,"cache_read_input_tokens":54960,"output_tokens":297,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":85},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2390},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":54960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2390,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HDB2NQv1N1xjwkdxxtfYYN":{"command":"which sr-checks; sr-checks run --help 2>&1 | head -30; ls ~/.local/share/cursor-agent/versions/"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cffebp6xTq2o8r1zhp3QH","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a67a4cd2-dbfa-4ffb-b536-d12ef97f1014","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:51:07.329Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"bae38a40-3d47-4493-bd0f-e501565b0fe6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YJFMUAjeHWM7erWfRFk4bt","type":"tool_result","content":"statement: >-\n  A hook command's exit status classifies its outcome: accepted (0), blocked\n  (2, with the hook's stderr as its message when it gave no other reason), or a\n  non-blocking error (any other status, except on WorktreeCreate, where any\n  non-zero status fails the creation, and except, in a harness that reads a\n  hook's output whatever its status, when stdout holds valid JSON, which alone\n  decides the outcome), after which the action goes on, unless the harness\n  has a setting that makes a hook's failures (a non-zero status, a crash, no\n  output) block the action instead. What a\n  block does on each event, how accepted output is used (context, decisions,\n  updated input) and hook timeouts are those events' and hook output's own\n  capabilities.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-output\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-2-behavior-per-event\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#other-exit-codes\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-json\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked-suppressed\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-unstartable\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock fires SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse,\n          PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure, Stop, SubagentStart, SubagentStop,\n          PreCompact, PostCompact, SessionEnd, WorktreeCreate and\n          WorktreeRemove, and no others. The docs' exit-code rows for StopFailure (which\n          the mock defines but never fires), ConfigChange,\n          CwdChanged, DirectoryAdded, Elicitation, ElicitationResult,\n          FileChanged, InstructionsLoaded, MessageDisplay, Notification,\n          PermissionDenied, PermissionRequest, PostModelSwitch, PostToolBatch,\n          PreModelSwitch, Setup, TaskCompleted, TaskCreated, TeammateIdle and\n          UserPromptExpansion are not modeled.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          A hook's JSON that fails Claude Code's output schema is a\n          non-blocking error in the mock too, whose message names the failing\n          field and carries the hook's own stderr, but not the full output\n          schema Claude Code prints after it. Only an invalid decision gives\n          Claude Code's recorded wording; any other field's complaint is the\n          mock's own.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          WorktreeRemove fails on a non-zero hook exit only if the worktree's\n          directory still exists afterward. The mock's worktree_remove manages\n          no directory, so any non-zero exit fails it.\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#pretooluse\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#userpromptsubmit\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#posttooluse\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#stop\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-json\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-unstartable\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/posttool-block\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock fires SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse,\n          PostToolUse and Stop, and no others. The docs' exit-code rows for\n          PermissionRequest, PreCompact, PostCompact, SubagentStart,\n          SubagentStop, Interrupt and SessionEnd are not modeled.\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#command-based-hooks\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#per-script-configuration-options\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#troubleshooting\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-fail-closed\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-json-nonzero\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock fires sessionStart, sessionEnd, preToolUse, postToolUse,\n          postToolUseFailure, beforeShellExecution, afterShellExecution and\n          afterFileEdit, and no others. The docs' exit-code rules for the other\n          permission hooks (beforeMCPExecution, beforeReadFile,\n          beforeTabFileRead, subagentStart) and for afterMCPExecution,\n          subagentStop, beforeSubmitPrompt, preCompact, stop,\n          afterAgentResponse, afterAgentThought, the Tab hooks and\n          workspaceOpen are not modeled; the recordings show cursor-agent in\n          print mode firing none of beforeSubmitPrompt, afterAgentResponse and\n          stop.\nstatement: >-\n  A hook fires when the session ends and says why; a non-interactive run\n  reports a generic reason. Whatever the hook prints is not recorded in the\n  transcript. (How long it may run is hook-timeout's, and which reasons a\n  configured matcher selects is hook-matcher-filter's.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#sessionend\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#sessionend-input\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The reasons clear, resume, logout and prompt_input_exit belong to an\n          interactive session (/clear, /resume, a logout, an exit from the\n          prompt). The mock models none, so every session ends with the\n          generic reason.\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#sessionend\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-end\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The docs name SessionEnd triggers of an app-managed thread: archiving\n          or deleting it, and 30 minutes of idleness. The mock models a\n          non-interactive run, which ends with its turn, so it fires SessionEnd\n          for that only.\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          That what the hook prints is not recorded in the transcript is not\n          shown for Codex: the docs say only that SessionEnd hooks are advisory\n          and their output does not steer Codex, and the recorded run's hook\n          prints nothing. The mock does not record it.\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#sessionend\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock has no interactive session, and models a run that ends by its\n          script's result, so the sessionEnd reasons window_close, user_close, aborted\n          and error, and the error message that goes with a reason of error, are not\n          modeled: it always says completed.\nstatement: >-\n  After a tool call succeeds, a hook fires with the tool's input, its\n  structured response and how long the call took. (What a particular tool's\n  response contains is that tool's own capability's.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#posttooluse\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#posttooluse-input\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#posttooluse\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/posttool-block\n    deviations:\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          Codex's PostToolUse payload does not say how long the call took: it\n          has no duration field, in its doc or in any recorded payload, and the\n          mock sends none.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock runs the shell tool and a sub-agent dispatch only, so what\n          PostToolUse reports for apply_patch, MCP tool calls and other local\n          function tools is not modeled.\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#posttooluse\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/file-tools\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/tool-failure\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock runs the Shell, Read and Write tools only, so what the MCP tools'\n          and the other tools' successful calls report to postToolUse is not modeled.\n          It times a command, but reports a duration of 0 for a file tool's call.\nstatement: >-\n  A hook fires each time the agent finishes responding. Its payload carries\n  the agent's last message, whether the agent is already continuing because an\n  earlier hook blocked, and the background tasks still running. (What those\n  tasks, and the scheduled wakeups the payload also lists, look like belongs\n  to their own capabilities.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#stop\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#stop-input\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgbash\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#stop\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n  cursor:\n    supported: false\n    reason: cursor-agent in print mode never fires the stop hook (the run configured one logging its payload), so no payload with a last message, continuation flag or background tasks is ever delivered.\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/stop-hook-payload\nstatement: >-\n  A hook fires before a submitted prompt reaches the agent. It can add context\n  to the prompt or refuse it, but it cannot rewrite it. It also fires for a\n  background-task notification handed to the agent. (What an exit status\n  means is hook-exit-code-semantics', and how added context is kept is\n  hook-additional-context's.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#userpromptsubmit-input\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#userpromptsubmit-decision-control\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#what-a-blocked-prompt-leaves-behind\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked-json\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/midturn\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#userpromptsubmit\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked\n  cursor:\n    supported: false\n    reason: In print mode cursor-agent never fires a configured beforeSubmitPrompt hook; one that tries to refuse the prompt is not run and the prompt reaches the agent, which acts on it.\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/user-prompt-submit-hook\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9d335afe-c0ef-49e0-9d49-f8af4a4f03f8","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:51:08.021Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bae38a40-3d47-4493-bd0f-e501565b0fe6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"a67a4cd2-dbfa-4ffb-b536-d12ef97f1014","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HDB2NQv1N1xjwkdxxtfYYN","type":"tool_result","content":"/Users/nsviridenko/.local/bin/sr-checks\nJudge every file-guard over merge-base(--base, --head)..--head.\n\nEvery check (requirement, script, judge) is cached by content: one verdict per guard and subject, keyed\nby the rule hash, the subject, the content of its files and the citation quotes. A stored PASS is a hit and a stored FAIL with the same key is replayed (terminal until the\ninput changes): nothing is run. A miss runs the steps in order and stores the verdict, as one segment\nof the sloprail/checks branch, and pushed to origin when the repository has one. Prints each\nrefusal, and exits 1 when any rule refuses.\n\nRun it in the foreground and wait: it prints progress to stderr (a line per judge and per rule, and a\nheartbeat every 30s), so do not poll the process list. It is safe to run in parallel, in several\nworktrees at once: judges share a machine-wide limit (SLOPRAIL_JUDGE_SLOTS, default 8; a process waits for\na free slot), two runs judging the same check judge it once, and a second run of the same worktree and\nrange waits for the first and reuses its verdicts. The lock files are under the user cache dir\n(SLOPRAIL_LOCK_DIR overrides) and a killed run releases them.\n\nUsage:\n  sr-checks run --base <rev> --head <rev> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --base string   The base revision: a branch, tag or sha (required)\n      --head string   The head revision: a branch, tag or sha (required)\n  -h, --help          help for run\n2025.10.02-bd871ac\n2026.09.28-64d2043\n2026.10.01-e373342","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4b544025-f211-46e5-99ec-39557a6b4444","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:51:09.825Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a67a4cd2-dbfa-4ffb-b536-d12ef97f1014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
