{"parentUuid":"e5ac813e-555f-423b-9185-ec3551cedd8f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KAw7VhzfdXNUoYqnKmQ1aA","type":"tool_result","content":"hook.sh\nhooks.json\nprompt.txt\n#!/bin/sh\n# slow: a PreToolUse hook that outlives its 1 second timeout, leaves a\n# grandchild running and has printed a deny that must be discarded.\n# probe: after the tool call, whether that grandchild is still alive.\nIN=$(cat)\ncase \"$1\" in\n  slow)\n    sleep 30 &\n    echo $! >\"$TMPDIR/grandchild\"\n    echo '{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecision\":\"deny\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"TIMEOUT-DENY\"}}'\n    wait ;;\n  probe)\n    if kill -0 \"$(cat \"$TMPDIR/grandchild\")\" 2>/dev/null; then s=alive; else s=gone; fi\n    printf '{\"grandchild\":\"%s\"}\\n' \"$s\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\" ;;\nesac\nexit 0\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PreToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh slow\",\n            \"timeout\": 1\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"PostToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh probe\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\nMake every shell command its own separate tool call, never combined with another command or put in a script. Run exactly this shell command, once: echo one. Then reply only DONE.\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"77f55ad9-7ac0-49d7-b1be-f4cc8492a9f0","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:52:58.278Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e5ac813e-555f-423b-9185-ec3551cedd8f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"dd4331d1-2641-4755-99bf-921abe0c1bc5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WrDumK71TLqbXehjQ2rzP8","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# The ONLY writer of cursor-mock/snapshots/ (the snapshots-read-only gate\n# refuses every other write). Everything it writes is sealed; snapshots-current\n# refuses a snapshot whose seal does not match, so a hand edit is caught at the\n# commit even if it slipped past the gate.\n#\n#   capture.sh run <name>    run the scenario in runs/<name>/setup/ against the\n#                            real `cursor-agent`, and add a sample\n#   capture.sh doc <url>     freeze a doc page (e.g. https://cursor.com/docs/hooks):\n#                            its sha256 goes in the MANIFEST; its text only into a cache\n#                            under the git dir, never into the repo\n#   capture.sh drop <run> <ts>  remove one sample (a bad or non-hermetic capture)\n#   capture.sh all           re-capture every run and doc at the installed\n#                            cursor-agent's version, and set MANIFEST.version to it\n#\n# The version is cursor-agent's release date (`2026.09.28`): `--version` also\n# prints a build hash after it (`2026.09.28-64d2043`), which the schema's\n# version pattern does not take, so the hash is dropped.\n#\n# Login: cursor-agent has no environment-only login in this setup, so the fake\n# HOME links to the user's Keychains directory and nothing else (the same as\n# claude-mock's capture). No credential is copied into the fake HOME; the\n# email the login reports is nulled out of every payload before anything is\n# sealed. A CURSOR_API_KEY is never read or passed.\n#\n# A scenario is hand-authored, and only its setup/ is:\n#   runs/<name>/setup/prompt.txt       the prompt\n#   runs/<name>/setup/hooks.json       the project's .cursor/hooks.json\n#   runs/<name>/setup/*.sh             optional: the hook scripts, installed in .cursor/hooks/;\n#                                      hook.sh appends to $HOOK_LOG\n#   runs/<name>/setup/args             optional: extra cursor-agent flags, one per line\n#   runs/<name>/setup/env              optional: KEY=VALUE lines cursor-agent inherits on\n#                                      top of the hermetic env\nset -euo pipefail\nhere=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nmanifest=\"$here/MANIFEST.yaml\"\ndie() { echo \"capture.sh: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }\nversion() { yq -r '.version' \"$manifest\"; }\ninstalled() { cursor-agent --version | awk '{print $1}' | sed 's/-.*$//'; }\n# The first capture creates the MANIFEST, frozen at the installed version: it is\n# a snapshot file too, so nothing else may write it.\n[ -f \"$manifest\" ] || printf 'version: \"%s\"\\n' \"$(installed)\" >\"$manifest\"\n\n# seal DIR — SEAL lists the sha256 of every other file under DIR.\n# Written to SEAL.tmp and renamed only on success, so a SEAL always means a\n# complete sample (the cleanup trap relies on it).\nseal() { (cd \"$1\" && find . -type f ! -name 'SEAL*' | LC_ALL=C sort | xargs shasum -a 256 >SEAL.tmp && mv SEAL.tmp SEAL); }\n\n# normalize — hook payloads and stream frames into events.jsonl: what a\n# scenario did, without what differs between two captures of the same\nruns/hook-timeout:\nrun.yaml\nsamples\nsetup\n\nruns/hook-timeout/setup:\nhooks.json\nlog.sh\nprompt.txt\nslow.sh\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"beforeShellExecution\": [\n      { \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/slow.sh SLOWOPEN\", \"timeout\": 1, \"matcher\": \"SLOWOPEN\" },\n      { \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/slow.sh SLOWCLOSED\", \"timeout\": 1, \"failClosed\": true, \"matcher\": \"SLOWCLOSED\" }\n    ],\n    \"afterShellExecution\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/log.sh\" }],\n    \"postToolUseFailure\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/log.sh\" }]\n  }\n}\n#!/bin/sh\n# Every event logs its payload.\nIN=$(cat)\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$IN\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\"\nexit 0\nDo these as separate shell tool calls, one command per call, in order, whatever happens: 1) echo SLOWOPEN 2) echo SLOWCLOSED 3) sleep 4 4) echo FINE. If a call is refused, do not retry it or look for a workaround; go on to the next. Then reply only DONE.\n#!/bin/sh\n# Runs longer than its 1 s timeout, with a background child that would log\n# after 3 s, and prints a deny it would give if it got to finish.\ncat >/dev/null\necho \"{\\\"hook_ran\\\":\\\"$1\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"started\\\"}\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\"\n( sleep 3; echo \"{\\\"hook_ran\\\":\\\"$1\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"grandchild-finished\\\"}\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\" ) &\nsleep 5\necho '{\"permission\":\"deny\",\"user_message\":\"SLOW-DENY\"}'\necho \"{\\\"hook_ran\\\":\\\"$1\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"finished\\\"}\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\"\nexit 0\nversion: 2026.09.28\ncommand: cursor-agent -p --force --trust --model auto --output-format stream-json","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"491cc154-c354-4e59-8e9e-9369ec16dc69","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:52:58.303Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dd4331d1-2641-4755-99bf-921abe0c1bc5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
