ktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"5dff6575-007d-4418-a7bf-a8bc1bb83dd8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BDLEm5fScJCCeVZ7fYRPgM","type":"tool_result","content":"50-Cloud agents run command-based hooks from your repository. If you have hooks defined in `.cursor/hooks.json` at the root of your project, cloud agents pick them up and run them during their work.\n51-\n52:On Enterprise plans, cloud agents also run team hooks and enterprise-managed hooks configured through the [web dashboard](https://cursor.com/dashboard/team-content?section=hooks).\n53-\n54-Cloud agents sometimes begin in a read-only environment for early exploratory turns. Hooks do not run during those turns. They start once the agent has a writable environment.\n55-\n56-### Supported hooks\n57-\n58-The following hooks run in cloud agents:\n59-\n60-| Hook                   | Supported |\n61-| ---------------------- | --------- |\n62-| `beforeShellExecution` | Yes       |\n63-| `afterShellExecution`  | Yes       |\n64-| `beforeReadFile`       | Yes       |\n--\n92-\n93-- **Project hooks** (`.cursor/hooks.json` in your repo): Loaded and run during cloud agent work.\n94:- **Team hooks** (Enterprise): Distributed from the dashboard and run in cloud agents.\n95-- **Enterprise hooks** (Enterprise): System-wide managed hooks run in cloud agents.\n96-\n97:User-level hooks (`~/.cursor/hooks.json`) are not available in cloud agents. Cloud agent VMs don't have access to your local home directory configuration.\n98-\n99:[Self-Hosted Machines](https://cursor.com/docs/cloud-agent/self-hosted.md) workers (Pools and My Machines) run the same command-based project hooks, and on Enterprise also run team and enterprise-managed hooks. On those workers, `sessionStart` and `sessionEnd` fire when a session claims the worker and when that claim is released. See [Hooks on Pools](https://cursor.com/docs/cloud-agent/self-hosted/pool.md#hooks).\n100-\n101-### Execution type limits\n102-\n103-Cloud agents run **command-based hooks** only. Prompt-based hooks require authentication wiring between the hook and the agent loop, which isn't available in the cloud execution environment.\n104-\n105-## Quickstart\n106-\n107:Create a `hooks.json` file. You can create it at the project level (`<project>/.cursor/hooks.json`) or in your home directory (`~/.cursor/hooks.json`). Project-level hooks apply only to that specific project, while home directory hooks apply globally.\n108-\n109:### User hooks (\\~/.cursor/)\n110-\n111:For user-level hooks that apply globally, create `~/.cursor/hooks.json`:\n112-\n113-```json\n114-{\n115-  \"version\": 1,\n116-  \"hooks\": {\n117-    \"afterFileEdit\": [{ \"command\": \"./hooks/format.sh\" }]\n118-  }\n119-}\n120-```\n121-\n122:Create your hook script at `~/.cursor/hooks/format.sh`:\n123-\n124-```bash\n125-#!/bin/bash\n126-# Read input, do something, exit 0\n127-cat > /dev/null\n128-exit 0\n129-```\n130-\n131-Make it executable:\n132-\n133-```bash\n134:chmod +x ~/.cursor/hooks/format.sh\n135-```\n136-\n137-### Project hooks (.cursor/)\n138-\n139-For project-level hooks that apply to a specific repository, create `<project>/.cursor/hooks.json`:\n140-\n141-```json\n142-{\n143-  \"version\": 1,\n144-  \"hooks\": {\n145-    \"afterFileEdit\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/format.sh\" }]\n146-  }\n--\n225-## Examples\n226-\n227:The examples below use `./hooks/...` paths, which work for **user hooks** (`~/.cursor/hooks.json`) where scripts run from `~/.cursor/`. For **project hooks** (`<project>/.cursor/hooks.json`), use `.cursor/hooks/...` paths instead since scripts run from the project root.\n228-\n229-```json title=\"hooks.json\"\n230-{\n231-  \"version\": 1,\n232-  \"hooks\": {\n233-    \"sessionStart\": [\n234-      {\n235-        \"command\": \"./hooks/session-init.sh\"\n236-      }\n237-    ],\n238-    \"sessionEnd\": [\n239-      {\n--\n624-## Configuration\n625-\n626:Define hooks in a `hooks.json` file. Configuration can exist at multiple levels. All matching hooks from every source run, and Cursor merges their responses: any `deny` wins over `ask`, and `ask` wins over `allow`, regardless of source. `user_message` and `agent_message` values are concatenated. For other fields, such as `followup_message`, the last response wins. Responses merge in the priority order below, so for those fields a lower-priority source overrides a higher-priority one:\n627-\n628-```sh\n629:~/.cursor/\n630-├── hooks.json\n631-└── hooks/\n632-    ├── audit.sh\n633-    └── block-git.sh\n634-```\n635-\n636-- **Enterprise** (MDM-managed, system-wide):\n637-  - macOS: `/Library/Application Support/Cursor/hooks.json`\n638-  - Linux/WSL: `/etc/cursor/hooks.json`\n639-  - Windows: `C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\Cursor\\\\hooks.json`\n640:- **Team** (Cloud-distributed, enterprise only):\n641-  - Configured in the [web dashboard](https://cursor.com/dashboard/team-content?section=hooks) and synced to all team members automatically\n642-- **Project** (Project-specific):\n643-  - `<project-root>/.cursor/hooks.json`\n644-  - Project hooks run in any trusted workspace and are checked into version control with your project\n645-- **User** (User-specific):\n646:  - `~/.cursor/hooks.json`\n647-\n648:Priority order (highest to lowest): Enterprise → Team → Project → User\n649-\n650-The `hooks` object maps hook names to arrays of hook definitions. Each definition currently supports a `command` property that can be a shell string, an absolute path, or a relative path. The working directory depends on the hook source:\n651-\n652-- **Project hooks** (`.cursor/hooks.json` in a repository): Run from the **project root**\n653:- **User hooks** (`~/.cursor/hooks.json`): Run from `~/.cursor/`\n654-- **Enterprise hooks** (system-wide config): Run from the enterprise config directory\n655-- **Team hooks** (cloud-distributed): Run from the managed hooks directory","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"65f50e0f-da1b-4ff8-8438-028c58f95af7","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:55:32.565Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5dff6575-007d-4418-a7bf-a8bc1bb83dd8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
