as no deviation for `failClosed`. The statement says that on timeout 'the event carries on', but Cursor's doc table says `failClosed: When true, hook failures (crash, timeout, ...) block the action instead of allowing it through`. The hook-timeout recording confirms it: the SLOWCLOSED hook timed out, so postToolUseFailure reported 'Hook script timed out after 1000ms' and the shell call ended 'rejected'. The cell has no `deviations` entry for this, whereas the Claude cell lists its analogous timeout-blocks case as a deviation. The other parts hold. The `timeout` option is documented as 'Execution timeout in seconds'. In the SLOWOPEN run the hook's output and grandchild never appear in the log, the deny is discarded, and the command succeeds. In the early-output run the EARLY-DENY printed before the timeout is discarded and the command succeeds.\nThe files this refusal is about: spec/capabilities/hook-common-payload.yaml, spec/capabilities/hook-timeout.yaml, spec/capabilities/hooks-all-matching-run.yaml, spec/capabilities/session-end-hook.yaml (file-guard \"capability-grounded\")\n  - No test pins the value of the mock's own cwd. The recordings show cwd \"\" on Shell events, but common_payload_fields_test.go asserts cwd == \"\" only on the recorded payloads. For the mock's payloads it compares only whether a cwd key is present, and replay_test.go:42 drops cwd from the conforms comparison. A mock that emitted cwd \"/some/dir\" on Shell events would still pass. Add an assertion on the mock's got.raw cwd values.\nThe files this refusal is about: cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/common_payload_fields_test.go, cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/session_end_output_test.go, cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/timeout_output_test.go, cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/two_sources_test.go, cursor-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, cursor-mock/snapshots/capture.sh, cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout-early-output/run.yaml, cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout-early-output/samples/20261003-165402/SEAL, cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout-early-output/samples/20261003-165402/events.jsonl, cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout-early-output/samples/20261003-165402/exit.txt (and 34 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The sessionEnd payload's duration_ms field is documented (total session duration in ms) and recorded (session-end-hook-output payloads.jsonl shows duration_ms:11068), but no test asserts it: replay_test.go normalizes it away and the cursor mock source has no duration_ms for sessionEnd, so add a test (and make the mock emit a numeric duration_ms). The rest is covered: reason and final_status completed, is_background_agent false, the hook firing once and last, and hook output kept out of the transcript. The other reasons are a declared deviation.\nThe files this refusal is about: cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/common_payload_fields_test.go, cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/session_end_output_test.go, cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/timeout_output_test.go, cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/two_sources_test.go, cursor-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, cursor-mock/snapshots/capture.sh, cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout-early-output/run.yaml, cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout-early-output/samples/20261003-165402/SEAL, cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout-early-output/samples/20261003-165402/events.jsonl, cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout-early-output/samples/20261003-165402/exit.txt (and 34 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ddeb2b72-a1db-4545-b8f3-1ffc8aadaec9","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:16:46.926Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"66e4406e-7076-4c2c-88f6-8a2dc330d915","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b"}
