{"parentUuid":"b104e7f9-b90f-4a74-b7c5-995a695faad7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VFerf3n1qnVFrnZqtJEmDu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\nsloprail: file-guards evaluated in 2m36.838s (26 rules, concurrency 6)\nTwo gaps. (1) The doc states a UserPromptSubmit hook can add context as JSON hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext (hooks#userpromptsubmit), but no test marked sr:proves user-prompt-submit-hook/codex exercises that form; they only use plain-text stdout (BANANA / CTX-FROM-PROMPT-HOOK), and the JSON form is checked only under hook-additional-context. (2) The refusal tests are too loose on the mock side: the recording (user-prompt-submit-hook-json-block) asserts the reason 'PROMPT-REFUSED-BY-JSON' is absent from the rollout, but TestAPromptRefusedByJSONRunsNothingAndSaysNothing asserts only that SHOULDNOTRUN is absent from the mock's rollout, and TestARefusedPromptRunsNothingAndSaysNothing never checks that the exit-2 stderr reason 'PROMPT-BLOCK-MSG' stays out of the rollout, so a mock that leaked the refusal reason to the agent would pass.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/prompt_hook_recorded_test.go, codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/prompt_json_block_test.go, codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/session_end_output_test.go, codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/stop_last_message_test.go, codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/stop_prompt_recorded_test.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-end-hook-output/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-end-hook-output/samples/20261003-165751/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-end-hook-output/samples/20261003-165751/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-end-hook-output/samples/20261003-165751/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-end-hook-output/samples/20261003-165751/payloads.jsonl (and 43 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7cff337b-2126-4