{"parentUuid":"cc698fc7-c8b6-45a6-b120-1a7f4a3085f6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a63bb90a3bc6561be","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffn5qtD6ShX2BX139WiJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both PRs are merged: cursor #119 and codex #124. All CI checks passed on the last head of each, and `sr-checks` came back with no refusals on all eight pairs. #119 first failed on one codex e2e test (`collab_test.go`), which I didn't change and passed on rerun.\n\n**Cursor (#119)**\n- **hook-timeout/cursor:**\n  - Flagged: the \"output is discarded\" part wasn't shown, because `slow.sh` only prints after the timeout.\n  - Changed: recorded `runs/hook-timeout-early-output`, where the hook prints a deny before its 1 s timeout. Real cursor discards the deny and runs the command. New replay test.\n  - The judge also found the `failClosed` timeout (it blocks the call, per `runs/hook-timeout`) undeclared, so I added a capability-grounding deviation.\n- **hooks-all-matching-run/cursor:**\n  - Recorded `runs/hooks-all-matching-run-same-hook-two-sources`. The same command in `~/.cursor/hooks.json` and the project's `hooks.json` ran twice, once per source, so cursor does not dedupe.\n  - Added an optional `user-hooks.json` to `capture.sh` for that recording.\n  - Added a capability-grounding deviation, plus a test pairing the recording with the mock reading the project source only.\n- **session-end-hook/cursor:**\n  - Recorded `runs/session-end-hook-output`: a `sessionEnd` hook printing on stdout, stderr and JSON. None of it reached the transcript, the stream or stderr.\n  - New test, which also pins the `duration_ms` and `final_status` fields the judge asked about.\n- **hook-common-payload/cursor:**\n  - The recordings show `workspace_roots` on every event, `cwd` only on Shell-tool events (always empty), and `transcript_path` null at `sessionStart`.\n  - The mock sent `cwd` on Read, Write and Task events too, which differs from the recording. I fixed the mock and added a test of the recorded fields.\n  - Added a capability-grounding deviation for the `workspace_roots` and null-transcript differences, and a modeled-surface one for `workspaceOpen` and transcripts-disabled.\n\n**Codex (#124)**\n- **hook-exit-code-semantics/codex:** `runs/hook-exit-json` shows exit 2 using stderr even beside a JSON reason. The mock already did this, so I only added a capability-grounding deviation stating it.\n- **user-prompt-submit-hook/codex:**\n  - Three new runs, each with replay tests:\n    - `user-prompt-submit-hook-rewrite`: a hook trying to rewrite the prompt has no effect.\n    - `user-prompt-submit-hook-bg`: a background command, and the hook fires once.\n    - `user-prompt-submit-hook-json-block`: a JSON block refuses the prompt like exit 2.\n  - Added a capability-grounding deviation: codex hands the agent no background-task notification.\n  - Added tests that refusal reasons stay out of the rollout and that JSON `additionalContext` reaches the agent.\n- **stop-hook-payload/codex:** I recorded `user-prompt-submit-hook-bg` and added tests pinning all three recorded Stops and their messages. Another agent landed the \"no background tasks\" deviation first, so I kept theirs.\n- **session-end-hook/codex:** another agent had already merged a `session-end-hook-output` run with the same name and the same recording, so I dropped mine and kept theirs.\n- **posttooluse-payload/codex:** main's cell already carried the capability-grounding deviation for the missing duration. The final `sr-checks` run raised nothing on it, so I changed nothing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":143,"cache_read_input_tokens":242825,"output_tokens":1269,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_